.TH "YAMLR-AUDIT" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBForensic Compliance, CIS Benchmark & Security Audit\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr audit\fR command conducts deep forensic compliance audits on Kubernetes manifests. It audits workloads against the Center for Internet Security (CIS) Kubernetes benchmarks, an embedded deprecation database, and high-entropy secret leakage detectors.
.PP
Execution is strictly read-only and local: manifests are analyzed in memory without modifying files on disk.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Audit manifests in the current directory
yamlr audit .

# Audit a specific manifest file
yamlr audit ./deploy/production.yaml

# Output audit findings in JSON
yamlr audit ./manifests -o json

# Export SARIF for GitHub Security code scanning
yamlr audit ./k8s -o sarif
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.SS "Positional Arguments"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB[PATH]\fR: Manifest file or directory to audit (defaults to \fB.\fR).
.SS "Output Formatting"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-o, --output <FORMAT>\fR: Output format (\fBtext\fR, \fBjson\fR, \fBsarif\fR). Defaults to \fBtext\fR.
.SH "AUDIT SCOPE & SECURITY RULES"
The audit engine inspects:
.PP
1. \fBCIS Kubernetes Benchmarks\fR: Checks for privileged containers, missing security contexts, host namespace sharing (\fBhostPID\fR, \fBhostIPC\fR, \fBhostNetwork\fR), and root execution (\fBrunAsNonRoot\fR).
.PP
2. \fBKubernetes API Deprecations\fR: Detects retired or deprecated API groups across Kubernetes releases.
.PP
3. \fBSecret Leakage Detection\fR: Scans manifests for plain-text credentials, high-entropy API tokens, private keys, and hardcoded connection strings.
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): Zero compliance findings or policy violations detected.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB1\fR (\fBEXIT_VIOLATIONS\fR): One or more audit violations or security findings were identified.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB2\fR (\fBEXIT_USAGE\fR): Invalid arguments or unsupported output format.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB124\fR (\fBEXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR\fR): Target unreadable or I/O failure.
